# Where the "Book a Demo" form sends.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill ONE of the two in. Vite only exposes
# variables prefixed `VITE_`, and it reads them at BUILD time — change one and
# the site has to be rebuilt for it to take effect.
#
# `.env` is already ignored by git (`*.local` is not enough, so check before
# committing). Neither value below is a secret in the usual sense: both ship
# inside the built JavaScript, because the browser is what posts to them. Use a
# key that is scoped to this form and nothing else.

# 1. Web3Forms — the shortest path, and no account to create.
#
#    Go to https://web3forms.com, enter info@youxel.com, and the access key is
#    emailed to that address. Paste it here. Submissions then arrive as email in
#    that inbox, with the sender's address set as the reply-to, so answering the
#    email answers the person.
VITE_DEMO_ACCESS_KEY=

# 2. Any other endpoint that accepts a JSON POST — a Formspree form
#    (https://formspree.io/f/xxxxxxx), a serverless function, your own API.
#    Set this and it wins over the key above.
# VITE_DEMO_ENDPOINT=
